    "method": "Fixed archive-admission check/wait timing on the sliding-control a10215e runtime. No admission, durability, retry or queue policy changes. The earlier control-sliding-candidate cohort is a historical reference, not a matched performance control. The benchmark VM now also mounts a scoped archive containing preserved stopped node data; fresh node volumes remain on the original internal filesystem. Fresh persistent host node volumes through Colima virtiofs and external RustFS on the 288-GiB VM disk. Cold benchmark VM restart per cohort. Three nodes, 1 vCPU and 3 GiB each, 500 leaders and 1000 followers each, 1500 groups/3 voters, four SQL workers with 16 slots each (64 total), four archive retained-cut slots. Two 180-second windows at 24 writers. Same load AST. Quorum acknowledgements, exact 4500 replica values and 1500 archive positions; timed mutations never retry. Shared-host activity recorded; existing cumulative metrics and cgroup CPU counters are sampled outside each timed load process; this task performs no builds or profiling during timing. Compare sustained throughput and p99 without converting reconciliation into a timed pass.",
